    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "We all know smoking and secondhand smoke are harmful. But have you heard of thirdhand smoke?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "When people smoke, harmful chemicals from the smoke stick to walls, clothes, and other surfaces long after the smoke is gone. This is called thirdhand smoke. Experts say it may also be dangerous to our health."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Doctors are studying thirdhand smoke to understand why some non-smokers still get lung cancer. A 2013 lab study showed it could even damage human DNA, which might increase the risk of disease."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Thirdhand smoke can stay for weeks, months, or even years. It can’t be removed by simply opening windows. What’s more, when "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "nicotine",
            "zh": "尼古丁"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in the smoke "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "reacts"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " with air, it can form cancer-causing "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "substances",
            "ref": "v-substance"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Although it’s hard to prove that it directly causes diseases, we should still be careful. Babies and young children are at higher risk because they often touch objects and then put their hands in their mouths. Pets may also be "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "affected",
            "ref": "v-affect"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " when they lick their fur."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "It’s important to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "be aware of",
            "ref": "v-be-aware-of"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " this hidden danger and try to avoid it."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ],
